@startuml Contest State Diagram
title Contest - State Transitions
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor<<initial>> LightBlue
  BackgroundColor<<active>> LightGreen
  BackgroundColor<<terminal>> LightGray
}

state "DRAFT" as DRAFT <<initial>>
state "ACTIVE" as ACTIVE <<active>>
state "UPCOMING" as UPCOMING
state "ENDED" as ENDED
state "COMPLETED" as COMPLETED <<terminal>>

note right of DRAFT
  **Default/Initial State**
  Set on creation via
  staffs.service.ts → createContest()
  status = createContestDto.status || DRAFT
end note

[*] --> DRAFT : createContest()\n[staffs.service.ts L117]

DRAFT --> ACTIVE : publishContest()\n[staffs.service.ts L308]\n(only from DRAFT, validates config)

DRAFT --> ENDED : Cron: handleEndedContests()\n[contest-cron.service.ts L39]\n(endDate <= today midnight)

UPCOMING --> ACTIVE : Cron: handleActiveContests()\n[contest-cron.service.ts L115]\n(startDate <= today <= endDate,\nruns EVERY_HOUR)

UPCOMING --> ENDED : Cron: handleEndedContests()\n[contest-cron.service.ts L35]\n(endDate <= today midnight,\nruns EVERY_DAY_AT_MIDNIGHT)

ACTIVE --> ENDED : Cron: handleEndedContests()\n[contest-cron.service.ts L31]\n(endDate <= today midnight,\nruns EVERY_DAY_AT_MIDNIGHT)

note bottom of COMPLETED
  No code path transitions
  TO ContestStatus.COMPLETED.
  Enum exists but is unused
  in current codebase.
  Possibly manual DB update
  or future feature.
end note

@enduml
